            "review_title": "Review at Ốc Loan",
            "review_text": "Nomadicus\nBuffalo, NY720 contributions\n0\nGold Chains, Charcoal Smoke, and One Unforgettable Street Feast at Ốc Loan\nOct 2025 • Friends\nỐc Loan was a stop on our evening Ho Chi Minh City food tour, and I’m genuinely grateful it was included. This is the kind of place you hope to stumble into but rarely do without a guide.\n\nBefore we even sat down, our tour guide teased the story of the owner, known for running the floor dripping in gold. This was not an exaggeration. He was very much present, commanding the space in stacked gold chains and oversized golden vambraces on each forearm, part ringmaster, part local legend.\n\nThe place was absolutely packed, buzzing with energy. Multiple charcoal grills fired nonstop, sending smoke and aroma into the street, while a fresh seafood display sat front and center. You can point and choose your adventure or let the staff guide you through it, though there is a traditional menu if you prefer structure over spontaneity.\n\nWe dove into clams in lemongrass broth, beef noodles, and an assortment of grilled seafood, including snails. Every dish arrived fresh, boldly seasoned, and impeccably cleaned something that matters deeply with the types of shellfish they serve. While the gold-clad owner steals your attention, the true star is his wife in the kitchen. Her cooking anchors the chaos with skill and confidence, turning raw seafood into deeply satisfying plates.\n\nỐc Loan is everything you want from Vietnamese street food. Curbside seating, tiny plastic stools, family-run intensity, unusual ingredients, and flavors that feel both wild and precise. Add in the characters, the heat, and the nonstop action, and you’re left with a meal that’s as memorable as it is delicious.\n\nThis isn’t just a place to eat. It’s an experience, loud, smoky, joyful, and unmistakably local.\nRead more\nWritten December 7, 2025",
